			"color":"#322",
			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the unified Chinese celestial-palace realm derived from <Picture 1>, <Picture 2>, <Picture 3>, <Picture 4>, <Picture 5>, <Picture 6>, and <Picture 7>. It features monumental white-jade architecture, dark-red lacquered timber, restrained antique-gold ornament, carved dragon reliefs, ancient pine trees, suspended palaces, waterfalls, mirror-like stone floors, distant mountains, warm celestial sunrise, and a vast layered sea of clouds.\n<Subject 2> is the group of distant celestial inhabitants shown across the reference pictures, wearing elegant layered Han-style robes in pearl white, pale blue, muted gold, and restrained cinnabar red. Their long dark hair, elongated robe silhouettes, calm posture, and ceremonial movement remain graceful and coherent. Their faces remain distant and indistinct rather than becoming close-up characters.\n<Subject 3> is the white celestial phoenix in <Picture 2>, with coherent bird anatomy, layered ivory-white feathers, long flowing tail plumes, elegant controlled flight, and natural delayed feather motion.\n<Picture 3> is the opening-frame composition of [Shot 1], establishing the colossal heavenly gate, ancient tree, cloud sea, and three distant figures.\n<Picture 2> is the principal composition anchor for [Shot 2], defining the circular golden moon gate, enormous pale moon, pine tree, phoenix, distant mountains, and four figures.\n<Picture 4> is the principal composition anchor for [Shot 3], defining the monumental palace, dragon-headed waterfall, reflective terrace, cloud abyss, and red-robed walking figure.\n<Picture 6> is the final-frame continuity anchor for [Shot 4], showing the celestial garden terrace, robed figures, flowers, reflective floor, cloud sea, and distant red-and-gold palace.\n<Audio 1> is the first fifteen-second soundtrack reference for shot timing, musical rhythm, emotional pacing, dynamic development, and the transition from mystery to majestic revelation.\n\nsummary:\n[keyframe completion + reference generation + audio reference] The target is the first fifteen seconds of an exceptionally refined cinematic Chinese celestial-palace film generated from multiple still images, text direction, and <Audio 1>. It progresses from the monumental heavenly gate in <Picture 3>, through the moon-gate and phoenix tableau in <Picture 2>, to the dragon-waterfall palace in <Picture 4>, and ends on <Picture 6> as the continuity handoff to the second clip. <Picture 1>, <Picture 5>, and <Picture 7> reinforce the white-jade material system, spatial depth, ancient-pine silhouettes, costume language, and cloud-sea atmosphere without becoming additional shots.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears throughout): fully_preserved - retain the Chinese architectural language, white-jade and dark-red material system, restrained gold detailing, monumental scale, warm sunrise direction, carved surfaces, cloud depth, and reflective floors.\n<Subject 2> (appears throughout): partially_preserved - preserve the elegant Han-style robe silhouettes, restrained palette, calm ceremonial performance, and distant human scale while allowing figure placement to follow each anchored composition.\n<Subject 3> (appears in [Shot 2]): fully_preserved - retain the white plumage, long tail feathers, coherent anatomy, graceful silhouette, and controlled flight.\n<Picture 3> ([Shot 1] first frame): fully_preserved - preserve the gate scale, ancient-tree framing, cloud depth, lighting direction, and three-figure placement.\n<Picture 2> ([Shot 2] keyframe): fully_preserved - preserve the circular frame, giant moon, pine tree, phoenix, mountain silhouettes, reflective floor, and four figures.\n<Picture 4> ([Shot 3] keyframe): fully_preserved - preserve the palace, dragon waterfall, reflective terrace, red-robed figure, and spatial proportions.\n<Picture 6> ([Shot 4] last frame): fully_preserved - preserve the terrace composition, figures, flowers, palace orientation, reflections, and lighting as the exact continuity handoff.\n<Audio 1>: reference - use its tempo, phrasing, emotional progression, and dynamic rise as audiovisual conditioning without introducing an unrelated musical identity.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target uses high-end cinematic Chinese mythological fantasy with realistic architectural materials, physically plausible atmospheric depth, delicate volumetric sunrise, luminous but restrained white jade, dark-red timber, antique gold accents, soft blue-grey shadows, and elegant slow movement. Create a refined immortal atmosphere through layered translucent mist, slow silk-like cloud movement, faint backlit moisture, soft light shafts, subtle atmospheric halos, and gently floating robe hems. The atmosphere must feel sacred, weightless, and visually expensive rather than decorative or artificial. Use <Picture 1>, <Picture 5>, and <Picture 7> only to reinforce architectural materials, spatial scale, pine silhouettes, cloud depth, and costume design. Do not create independent shots from those supporting pictures.\n\n[Shot 1] Begin exactly from <Picture 3>. A colossal carved white-jade heavenly gate rises from an endless cloud sea, framed by the dark trunk and layered branches of an ancient pine. Three distant members of <Subject 2> stand quietly on the cliffside terrace facing the gate. During 00:00.000–00:05.000, the camera performs an extremely slow forward dolly combined with a slight rightward drift. Foreground branches, figures, drifting mist, cloud layers, and distant architecture create restrained natural parallax. Thin translucent cloud ribbons pass below the terrace. Soft sunrise rays travel through the mist and gently reveal the carved relief. The jade absorbs and diffuses light subtly instead of glowing like plastic. Robe hems, hair ribbons, and hanging foliage move slowly in the high-altitude breeze.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:05.000, a thin foreground cloud veil crosses the lens and reveals <Picture 2>. The camera begins wide and slowly pushes toward the enormous circular golden moon gate. The pale moon remains softly luminous with visible surface texture and no overexposure. <Subject 3> crosses the upper-left portion of the golden circle from left to right with two measured wing beats. Its long tail feathers follow with smooth delayed motion and catch a faint pearlescent rim light. Four members of <Subject 2> walk slowly along the lower-right terrace. Their sleeves and robe trains float gently without exaggerated wind. The pine tree, moon gate, mountains, reflective floor, and architectural edges remain structurally stable.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:10.000, luminous waterfall mist briefly fills the foreground and clears into <Picture 4>. The camera tracks slowly from left to right beside the red-robed figure while preserving the dragon-headed waterfall and palace as the dominant subjects. Water falls with realistic weight, separating into fine translucent veils near the cloud layer. A restrained rainbow-like halo appears only inside the backlit mist. The red robe train follows naturally across the reflective terrace. The palace columns, carved dragons, rooflines, and terrace edges remain sharp, massive, and immovable.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:13.200, the waterfall mist thickens into a soft natural transition and clears into <Picture 6>. The camera settles into an almost-static wide terrace view. Flowers and hanging vines move subtly, low mist glides across the reflective floor, and distant clouds drift behind the palace. Preserve the figures, garden, palace orientation, reflections, sunrise direction, and spatial continuity. Hold the final composition steadily through 00:15.000.\n\nGlobal negative constraints: no subtitles, logos, watermarks, random writing, pseudo-Chinese characters, Western castles, Japanese shrine elements, neon science-fiction lighting, cheap blue or gold glow, magical energy beams, glitter storms, particle accumulation, excessive lens flare, plastic CGI materials, oversharpening, oversaturation, boiling clouds, duplicated people, malformed limbs, facial mutation, unstable costumes, melting architecture, bending columns, roof deformation, temporal flicker, camera shake, rapid flight, sudden zooms, or abrupt exposure changes.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nSoft high-altitude wind, distant layered waterfall resonance, restrained robe and foliage movement, one subtle phoenix wing passage, and faint bronze chimes remain secondary to <Audio 1>. The environment feels vast and quiet. No dialogue, narration, crowd chatter, thunder, impact sounds, or prominent artificial effects.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nFollow the tempo, instrumental character, phrasing, emotional progression, and dynamic rise of <Audio 1>. Preserve its ethereal and majestic quality without introducing a separate melody, vocal layer, heavy percussion, trailer-style impact, or unrelated rhythmic pattern."
